<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Penda of Mercia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 655</span> · Also known as Penda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Penda was the pagan king of Mercia who made it the strongest kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midlands">English Midlands</a> in the mid-7th century. Allied with Welsh rulers, he killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edwin-of-northumbria">Edwin of Northumbria</a> at Hatfield Chase in 633 and Oswald at Maserfield in 642, and he defeated East Anglia and drove the king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a> into exile. He was killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiu">Oswiu of Northumbria</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-winwaed">Battle of the Winwaed</a> in 655.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia.jpg" alt="Penda of Mercia" width="320" height="581" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Violetriga · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Penda_of_Mercia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
